      "result": "\n\nWrote `submission/main.c` with the complete Zephyr UART echo application:\n\n- **Device lookup** — `DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_ALIAS(uart0))` at file scope inside `main()`, as a `const struct device *const` (matches Zephyr's `DEVICE_DT_GET` const-qualifier behavior).\n- **Readiness check** — `device_is_ready(uart)` before any use; returns `-ENODEV` if the device isn't ready.\n- **Polling loop** — a tight `while (true)` loop with no sleep; `uart_poll_in(uart, &byte)` is called every iteration and the byte is only echoed via `uart_poll_out(uart, byte)` when the read succeeds (return value `0`). A negative return (no data) just loops back to poll again.\n- **Headers** — `zephyr/kernel.h` and `zephyr/drivers/uart.h`.\n\n```c\nconst struct device *const uart = DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_ALIAS(uart0));\n\nif (!device_is_ready(uart)) {\n    return -ENODEV;\n}\n\nuint8_t byte;\n\nwhile (true) {\n    if (uart_poll_in(uart, &byte) == 0) {\n        uart_poll_out(uart, byte);\n    }\n}\n```",
